---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="GIA Certification — What is GIA? | Novva Diamonds"
  description="Learn about GIA (Gemological Institute of America) diamond certification. Understand why GIA grading is the gold standard and how to read a GIA certificate."
>
  <nav class="bg-surface border-b border-muted" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <div class="container-luxe py-4">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-caption text-text-light">
        <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-accent transition-colors">Home</a></li>
        <li><span class="mx-1">/</span></li>
        <li><a href="/education/" class="hover:text-accent transition-colors">Education</a></li>
        <li><span class="mx-1">/</span></li>
        <li class="text-on-surface font-semibold">GIA Certification</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <article class="section-padding bg-surface-warm">
    <div class="container-narrow rich-text">
      <div class="text-center mb-16 reveal">
        <span class="overline block mb-4">Diamond Education</span>
        <h1 class="text-headline-lg mb-4" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);">GIA Certification</h1>
        <hr class="divider-gold mx-auto mb-6" />
        <p class="text-body-lg text-text-light max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          The Gemological Institute of America (GIA) is the world's foremost authority in gemology.
          A GIA certificate is the gold standard in diamond grading.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12 reveal">
        <h2>What is GIA?</h2>
        <p>
          Founded in 1931, the <strong>Gemological Institute of America (GIA)</strong> is a nonprofit organization
          dedicated to research and education in the field of gemology. GIA created the universally accepted
          standard for describing diamonds — the 4Cs of diamond quality — and the International Diamond Grading System™.
        </p>
        <p>
          GIA is regarded as the world's most trusted name in diamond grading and gem identification because of their
          consistency, unbiased approach, and scientific rigor. They do not buy, sell, or trade diamonds, ensuring
          complete objectivity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12 reveal">
        <h2>Why GIA Certification Matters</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Unbiased and Independent:</strong> GIA does not buy or sell diamonds, so their grading is free from commercial influence.</li>
          <li><strong>Consistent Standards:</strong> Every diamond is graded by multiple gemologists using the same strict criteria.</li>
          <li><strong>Global Recognition:</strong> GIA certificates are recognized and trusted by jewelers, retailers, and consumers worldwide.</li>
          <li><strong>Comprehensive Reporting:</strong> Each report includes a detailed analysis of the 4Cs plus additional quality characteristics.</li>
          <li><strong>Laser Inscription:</strong> Many GIA-graded diamonds have their report number microscopically laser-inscribed on the girdle for identification.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12 reveal">
        <h2>How to Read a GIA Certificate</h2>
        <p>A GIA Diamond Grading Report includes:</p>
        <div class="bg-surface border border-muted rounded-md overflow-hidden my-6">
          {[
            { field: "Report Number", desc: "Unique identification number for the diamond and its report" },
            { field: "Shape and Cutting Style", desc: "The diamond's shape (Round, Oval, etc.) and faceting pattern" },
            { field: "Measurements", desc: "The diamond's dimensions in millimeters" },
            { field: "Carat Weight", desc: "The diamond's weight measured to the hundredth of a carat" },
            { field: "Color Grade", desc: "The absence of color, graded on a scale from D (colorless) to Z" },
            { field: "Clarity Grade", desc: "The absence of inclusions and blemishes" },
            { field: "Cut Grade", desc: "How well the diamond's facets interact with light (for round brilliants)" },
            { field: "Polish & Symmetry", desc: "Quality of the surface finish and facet alignment" },
            { field: "Fluorescence", desc: "The diamond's reaction to UV light" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4 px-6 py-4 border-b border-muted last:border-0">
              <span class="text-label-md text-accent min-w-[140px] pt-0.5">{item.field}</span>
              <span class="text-body-sm text-text-light">{item.desc}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12 reveal">
        <h2>Verifying a GIA Certificate</h2>
        <p>
          Every GIA report can be verified online at <strong>gia.edu</strong> using the report number. This ensures the
          authenticity of the certificate and confirms that the diamond's grading has not been altered.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Novva Diamonds, every GIA-certified diamond in our collection comes with its complete certificate number.
          We encourage buyers to verify each diamond independently before making a decision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="text-center py-8 reveal">
        <hr class="divider-gold mx-auto mb-8" />
        <h2 class="text-headline-md mb-4">Browse GIA Certified Diamonds</h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-text-light mb-8 max-w-lg mx-auto">
          Explore our collection of GIA certified loose diamonds with full grading details.
        </p>
        <a href="/diamonds/?cert=GIA" class="btn btn-primary">View GIA Diamonds</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
